libc — newlib's hand-written R5900 string/memory routines, linked as library members
====================================================================================

Why this directory exists
-------------------------
Six functions in the game's SDK code are newlib libc routines that the SDK
built from hand-written assembly, not C. Each SDK libc.a object's stabs name
src/newlib/libc/machine/r5900/<name>.S (FACT #9816). This directory holds those
.S files verbatim, and tools/ee/build_libgcc.sh assembles them as library
members (RULING #9817, under RULING #9783), so the game's units no longer carry
their bodies as INCLUDE_ASM. They were never C, so this is not decompilation.
It is the original source, built by the original assembler.

Nothing here is edited. If a file's verbatim source does not assemble to the
ROM's bytes, that member stays INCLUDE_ASM in its game unit.

