How each member is built and checked
------------------------------------
going-decompiled/libgcc/MEMBERS has one row per member (source column ends in
`.S`). build_libgcc.sh runs the SDK cpp.exe with -lang-asm and the same
predefines as the C members, then assembles the whole file with the held SN
Ps2EeAs.exe 1.9.25.758, the SDK's own assembler. Per RULING #9817, each linked
member was checked two ways:
  - Ps2EeAs output vs the ROM: byte-identical over the function's size, at its
    address, in USA and in EU.
  - The held EE gas (as.exe 2.9-ee-991111b) on the same input vs the SDK
    libc.a member: identical .text sha1.

The assembler is load-bearing, measured. For strcmp, strlen and strncpy, EE gas
does NOT reproduce the ROM: it gives the SDK archive's bytes, which are 2, 4
and 4 words shorter. The source writes its byte-mask constants as
`dli $7,0x0101010101010101` / `dli $6,0x8080808080808080`. EE gas expands
0x0101... from lui; Ps2EeAs derives it from the 0x8080... chain ending in
`dsll $7,$7,9; ori $7,$7,0x101`, one word more per site (10 sites, FACT #9823).
That one source tree yields two binaries is what was earlier recorded as
"revision skew". It is an assembler difference, not a source revision.

Placement: the ld-r group
-------------------------
memcmp, memcpy, memset and strcmp are contiguous in the ROM (0x115340..0x11568F),
each .text 4-aligned, and memcpy, memset and strcmp start at 4 mod 8. The game's
.cod output section is SUBALIGN(8), which would push each lone member to the
next 8 (measured: memcpy at 0x1153D8 instead of 0x1153D4). So MEMBERS links
them as one group, r5900_memcmp_strcmp: the four unmodified Ps2EeAs objects
combined by `ld -r` in ROM order. No relocation is edited and no padding is
added. The objects have no relocations, and the group's .text is their four
.text sections back to back. The group starts at 0x115340, 8-aligned, and ends
at 0x115690, 8-aligned.

strncpy is linked alone (0x115AC0..0x115C8F). Its Ps2EeAs .text is one word
longer than the function: a trailing zero word, which the ROM also holds at
0x115C8C.

strlen is vendored but NOT linked. It starts at 0x1157AC (4 mod 8) right after
game code (func_00115690), so it cannot be grouped with a library neighbour, and
SUBALIGN(8) forbids it alone. It stays INCLUDE_ASM in cod/015610 (task #1884).
